# A chest is eight planks in a ring on a 3x3 grid, so it needs a placed
# crafting table. Shaped exactly like `get_furnace`: goal, craft, input, table.
#
# Depth 2: get_chest -> get_planks (a leaf), and get_crafting_table_near (a
# leaf). Eight planks is two logs' worth (one log gives four), and `get_planks`
# mines its own logs, so this skill never calls `get_wood`.
#
# Why the rules are ordered this way: the goal check is on top. The craft rule
# asks for both things it cannot make itself (eight planks of any wood type and
# a table within reach). The plank rule under it fetches the planks, and a
# failed `get_planks` makes it ineligible for one tick, so the table rule gets
# its turn. The table rule is last because it is always true when nothing else
# is missing: `get_crafting_table_near` places the held table or crafts and
# places one, and returns done at once when a table already stands there, so
# `craft` above it can never fail `needs_table`.
skill get_chest()
  doc "Have a chest in the inventory: eight planks crafted at a placed crafting table."
  rules:
    count(chest) >= 1 -> done
    count(#planks) >= 8 and near(crafting_table, 4) -> craft(chest)
    count(#planks) < 8 -> do get_planks(8)
    true -> do get_crafting_table_near()
